sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 8, docs/reference/development-containers.md#sleep-and-wake): a request to the Route, a Conn device or a task turn wakes a stopped container. The runtime activation endpoint of docs/reference/app-dev-runtime-hibernation.md#wake starts the run.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · runtime activation
  %% kind: instance.wake
  autonumber
  %% lane CL icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CL as Caller<br/>Caddy, Conn, task
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant C as Container<br/>via incus exec
  CL->>GW: Wake the Instance<br/>GET runtime-activations
  %%> Callers:
  %%> - Caddy on the Instance's Node, when a request finds no awake marker
  %%> - a Conn device, when it opens the T3 server of a sleeping Instance
  %%> - the task flow, before a turn on an attached Instance
  %%> - a development deployment of a sleeping default Instance starts it within its own run
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the caller is the Instance's Node or has node access to it
  Note over GW: Start or join the wake<br/>one per Instance
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a second caller joins the running wake; Caddy gets the progress page, Conn and the task flow the task ID
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-wake
  GW-->>CL: Progress page · task ID
  SW->>N: Start the container<br/>incus start
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - nftables, T3, the app and the desired-running Processes start with the container
  SW->>C: Check T3 and Processes<br/>Ansible · tags check
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - waits up to 30 s for T3's environment endpoint and the Processes' units, else `instance.t3_unready`
  %%> - writes the awake marker
  opt the Gateway session expires within 7 days
    SW->>C: Issue the Gateway session<br/>sensitive output · vault
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - see container/t3-register.mmd
  end
  alt the run passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Record awake
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the runtime is `running`; the Conn layer shows the T3 server awake, and renews its session when a new one came
    %%> - the progress page loads the original path; Conn connects; the task sends its turn
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step, error_code
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the progress page shows the failure; the next request starts a new wake
  end
